3:T46b,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I arrange a home visit eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Contact a domiciliary optical practice in your area, ask your GP for a recommendation, or call NHS 111. Many high-street opticians also provide home visits for eligible patients. Your optician can check whether you qualify for a free NHS home visit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a home eye test as thorough as an in-practice test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. A domiciliary eye test meets the same clinical standards as a practice-based test. The optometrist uses portable versions of the same equipment and carries out all the same checks on your vision and eye health."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can someone in a care home have an eye test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Care home residents are typically eligible for free NHS home visit eye tests. Many domiciliary optical practices regularly visit care homes in their area. The care home manager or staff can arrange visits on behalf of residents."}}]}0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","$L2",null,{}],["$","main",null,{"className":"flex-1","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"Eye Tests at Home — Domiciliary Eye Care in the UK\",\"description\":\"If you cannot visit an optician, a qualified optometrist can carry out a full eye test in your own home. Learn about domiciliary eye care.\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk/find/eye-test-at-home\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"eyetest.co.uk\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"eyetest.co.uk\",\"url\":\"https://www.eyetest.co.uk\"},\"dateModified\":\"2026-06-16\",\"breadcrumb\":{\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"Li